    "gaps": [
      "This main projection excludes hub preflight/dry-run/launch/write-audit internals and the HubResult transport envelope. MCP tools enforce the service mutation gate for compiler, self-test and output writes.",
      "Admission specializes argv and the selected module list to at most 256; native source has no numeric cap. At 256 modules done is true on iteration 256, so normal completion wins; exhaustion is unreachable for admitted inputs with the authored bound.",
      "Context repository_root supplies the native repository/cwd mount; relative argv paths resolve there, and sorted legacy MathformerPhysicsLib/Lean/Foundations defaults are discovered on initialization of that mount. The direct CLI retains import-time DEFAULT_MODULES. Mounted defaults must fit 256 modules.",
      "The 3600-second/call budgets and required receipts are enforced by the Lunar host, not by native Lake; neither the original hub leaf nor Lake sets a timeout. Complete Lake/network effects need qualification. Tests substitute only the external compiler boundary.",
      "Native printed reports and argparse diagnostics are routed to MCP stderr to preserve protocol framing; Emission.text is the exact native serialized report.",
      "Lunar cannot compile branch-local loop exhaustion. The module loop is hoisted to the root sequence with a typed VerifyState carrier. retain_empty performs no module visit on empty input or after self-test; self_test_report unpacks the already-computed native report. Selected scans and all side effects retain native order."
    ]
  },
